From: Retrorerr <116828772+Retrorerr@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: glewInit: accept a context without a GLX display

GLEW built for GLX loads every GL entry point in glewContextInit() and only
then asks glxewInit() for GLX extensions, which fails with
GLEW_ERROR_NO_GLX_DISPLAY when the current context came from EGL: SDL2,
GLFW and friends on native Wayland. The caller sees glewInit() fail and
gives up on GL (HyperRogue draws a black window), although every GL
function it needs is loaded. A missing GLX display now only leaves the
GLX extension flags unset, as on an EGL build.

--- a/src/glew.c
+++ b/src/glew.c
@@ -23116,7 +23116,12 @@ GLenum GLEWAPIENTRY glewInit (void)
 #elif defined(_WIN32)
   return wglewInit();
 #elif !defined(__APPLE__) || defined(GLEW_APPLE_GLX) /* _UNIX */
-  return glxewInit();
+  /* The GL entry points are loaded by now. A context made current through
+   * EGL (native Wayland) has no GLX display: that only leaves the GLX
+   * extension flags unset.  */
+  r = glxewInit();
+  return r == GLEW_ERROR_NO_GLX_DISPLAY ? GLEW_OK : r;
 #else
   return r;
 #endif /* _WIN32 */
